Recommends: homelab-api, homelab-domain-admin, homelab-postfix-block-link, homelab-webproxy, homelab-audit, homelab-agent
Description: Click-to-block-from-inbox settings + public management page
 Owns the click-to-block-link mechanism's settings (a per-domain
 default, site_admin-set, plus a per-account self-service override) and
 the public /l/:token management page a recipient reaches via the link
 the companion package homelab-postfix-block-link injects into inbound
 mail. Fronted two ways from one process: /internal/v1/block-link/* via
 homelab-api's own /api/v1/block-link/* gateway route (JWT-
 authenticated, same shape as homelab-invite), and /l/:token on its own
 public webproxy vhost (unauthenticated -- see README.md's
 "Deployment" section).
 .
 Deliberately NOT a new blocking mechanism -- it's a new delivery path
 into the one that already exists. Clicking a link and submitting the
 form calls homelab-domain-admin's own recipient-access on-behalf
 endpoint (system_agent-authenticated, since the person clicking has no
 JWT of their own), writing to the SAME domainadmin.recipient_access
 table the recipient_blocking Roundcube plugin and `homelab-cli mail
 block` already use. This service never writes that table directly.
 .
 Management links are long-lived (default 90 days), not one-time-use
 -- a deliberate divergence from homelab-invite's own token design,
 since revisiting the same link later to adjust a decision is the
 normal, expected use here.
